    "text": "Contribution A draft, evidence-led documentation package for future teams to verify and build on — not a finished Registry contribution. Home Project Contribution 01 — Contribution What this draft actually offers Our contribution at this stage is documentation, not a finished product. It is an honest, evidence-led package that a future team could pick up and verify: a chronological audit of the 18 supplied records, the practical protocol observations that go with it, the explicit negative and inconclusive outcomes, and a clearly drawn line between preliminary PCR evidence and sequence-confirmed editing. To be clear about what this is not : we are not claiming a completed Registry contribution, a published dataset, a validated software or hardware tool, community adoption, a fully validated protocol set, or a working sensor. Those claims would require evidence the current records do not contain. 02 — The package What a future team can pick up 01 A dated experimental record Eighteen documented notebook records with a result status for each, including the dead ends. 02 Practical protocol observations Bench workflows as recorded, with the handling notes and the gaps that matter for reuse. 03 An evidence-status parts ledger Named elements and construct work, separated from the evidence still missing for each. These pages are working documentation, not final validated resources. They are most useful as a starting point to reproduce, correct, and extend — not as endpoints to cite. 03 — Draft vs. final What would make this a real contribution The gap between this draft and a contribution we could publish is concrete and worth naming explicitly. Already documented (draft) Required before a final contribution claim Chronological notebook with result status Confirmed sequences and Registry identifiers for each element Recorded bench workflows and handling notes Complete, reproducible protocols with programs and success criteria Explicit negative and inconclusive outcomes Complete source data behind the gels: some 0527/0530 records embed gel images, but uncropped and labelled images, expected sizes, and written interpretation are still missing Preliminary 0607 ΔGal80 PCR conclusion Independent validation and replication, including sequencing Element and construct names with documented work Clear licensing and versioning for reuse 04 — Scope Where we draw the line We are not presenting the underlying scientific idea — a yeast GPCR reading a nematode ascaroside signal — as an iGEM contribution. A hypothesis is not a reusable artifact, and the records do not yet contain a concrete, verified deliverable built on it. What we can offer honestly is the documentation package above, which is why this page remains hidden until its contents are verified. Why this page is still a draft A contribution claim is only as good as the evidence behind it. Until sequences, complete protocols, source data, and independent replication are in place, this stays a draft package to build on rather than a finished contribution to rely on.",
