    "text": "Safety The bench practices the records actually document — and the biosafety information still needed before this page can make compliance claims. Home Project Safety 01 — Documented What the records actually show The audited notebook documents a set of standard microbiology and molecular-biology practices. We describe them here as documented practices only — they are what the records show the team doing, not proof of full biosafety compliance, which would require the institutional information listed further down this page. Chassis handled Trans5α competent E. coli and S. cerevisiae CEN.PK2-1C, as named in the records. Bench practices Autoclaving wrapped, labelled vessels with indicator tape; aseptic hood and clean bench for plating and cell work. Recorded precautions Light and UV protection for tryptophan-containing material; minimal (~10 s) UV during gel excision; deliberate marker labelling. Also documented across the records: plasmid handling and minipreps, PCR and agarose-gel electrophoresis, and yeast transformation with dropout selection. None of these entries, on its own, demonstrates that a formal safety framework was in place. 02 — Gaps Biosafety information not yet in evidence The following would normally anchor a biosafety page. None of it is established in the supplied material, so we do not assert it, and we do not assign a risk group or biosafety level from general knowledge. Item Status in supplied evidence Institutional biosafety level Not supplied Biosafety training records Not supplied Supervision arrangements Not supplied Personal protective equipment Not supplied Decontamination and waste handling Not supplied Strain provenance and approvals Not supplied Antibiotic handling details Requires confirmation (see below) Genetic-part risk review Not supplied No risk-group or containment-level claim Because none of the above is documented, this page makes no institutional biosafety-level, risk-group, containment-approval, or waste-procedure claim. Those determinations belong to the host institution and are outstanding for this draft. 03 — Antibiotics An antibiotic value to confirm first The earliest records (0506 and 0507) state an ampicillin stock and working concentration that are atypical for standard LB–ampicillin selection and may reflect a unit error. The suspect values are not printed here. They must be confirmed with the team before any protocol or risk assessment that depends on antibiotic handling is finalised. The corresponding bench workflow is documented on the Protocols page, also with the numbers withheld. 04 — By design Containment and non-release as future requirements The intended direction of the project is a diagnostic that reads a soil-borne nematode signal rather than an organism released into the environment. That is a design intention, not a demonstrated safeguard: the current records show no direct-soil testing, environmental release, field deployment, or finished diagnostic enclosure. Non-release is a requirement, not a result Physical and biological containment and strict non-release would be requirements for any future implementation of this system. Nothing in the present records demonstrates them, so we describe them as design obligations to meet, not features already achieved. 05 — Risk Risks to weigh in future design Because no device has been built or tested, the following are prospective design risks rather than measured performance. A future assay would need to address the possibility of false positives and false negatives, and the specificity of the chosen biomarker: literature the team reviewed describes the candidate ascaroside as conserved across several related root-knot species, which may prevent species-level discrimination; its full taxonomic range and specificity remain untested. Turning that into a reliable readout — and defining any real-world sensitivity, specificity, or response behaviour — remains future design work. No measured device performance This page reports no detection limit, response time, sensitivity, specificity, or species discrimination. Those are not established by the records and are not claimed here.",
