        "id": "repo",
        "title": "Repository",
        "text": "06 - Repository Read the code Everything described above is in one repository, and the shortest way to check any of it is to read build.py from top to bottom. It is a single standard-library file, and every behaviour on this page is somewhere inside it. Use the visible Source repository link in the footer to inspect the build script, templates, page sources, design system, and interaction layer. On the official iGEM deployment this link is injected from GitLab's CI_PROJECT_URL . That link is ordinary page content. No script, stylesheet, font or image is fetched from it, or from any other off-site origin, while a page is being read - which is the entire point of building the site this way.",
